I reach the flat in the afternoon.
I go straight to my bedroom.
I take the new green shirt out of the bag.
I try that shirt on.
Then I look in the mirror.
I realize one thing immediately.
This shirt is very small.
It is smaller than my usual shirts.
It is very tight on my shoulders.
I cannot move my hands well.
The sizes of this brand are very small.
I need a bigger shirt than this.
Therefore, I take off the shirt.
I fold it like before.
I put it back in the bag along with the bill.
I decide to go back to the shop tomorrow morning.
I want to exchange this shirt.
I must go there and ask for a bigger one than this.
